[SIZE=6][B]MC Data Bridge - Detailed Documentation[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=5]► Configuration Breakdown[/SIZE]

Below is a detailed explanation of the [I]config.yml[/I] settings. This file is generated on each backend server (Paper/Spigot/Folia). Proxies (Bungee/Velocity) do not require a config file; they use internal defaults.

[SIZE=4][B]1. Database Connection[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]database.type:[/B] Use [CODE]mysql[/CODE] for external databases (MariaDB/MySQL) or [CODE]sqlite[/CODE] for local file-based storage.
[*][B]database.host/port/database:[/B] Standard credentials for your MySQL server.
[*][B]database.sqlite-file:[/B] The filename used if the type is set to [I]sqlite[/I].
[*][B]database.serialization-format:[/B] Use [CODE]json[/CODE] for backward-compatible Base64 JSON format, or [CODE]binary[/CODE] to store compressed NBT byte arrays, saving database storage and connection bandwidth.
[*][B]database.pool-settings:[/B] Advanced HikariCP settings. Defaults are highly optimized for resilience against network jitter.
[*][B]database.optimizations:[/B] Fine-tuned JDBC driver settings to ensure non-blocking performance.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]2. Core Identity & Security[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]server-id:[/B] [B]CRITICAL.[/B] Every server connected to the same database must have a unique identifier (e.g., "survival-1", "creative").
[*][B]security.seed:[/B] A secret string used to salt all SHA-256 hashes and identity checks. [B]If this is left as the default "change-me-to-a-long-random-string", the plugin will fail to start to prevent unauthorized network access.[/B]
[*][B]security.verify-data-integrity:[/B] When enabled, the plugin will reject data loads if the SHA-256 checksum does not match, protecting against database tampering.
[*][B]identity.mode:[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]PREMIUM:[/B] Strictly enforces UUID consistency. Blocks logins if a name is claimed by a different UUID.
[*][B]HYBRID:[/B] Allows for identity shifts (Name -> UUID), ideal for networks migrating from cracked to premium. [B]Note: HYBRID mode is required for auto-migration features (FastLogin/AuthMe).[/B]
[/LIST]
[*][B]identity.auto-migrate-fastlogin:[/B] If true, automatically transfers data to a player's premium account once FastLogin verifies their session.
[*][B]identity.auto-migrate-authme:[/B] If true, automatically transfers data to a player's premium account once they authenticate via AuthMe.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]3. Synchronization Control[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]sync-data:*:[/B] Individual toggles for every data type. You can sync just inventories but keep health local to each server, or vice versa (includes [CODE]maps[/CODE] and [CODE]separate-gamemode-inventories[/CODE]).
[*][B]maps.mode:[/B] Choose map synchronization mode: [CODE]return[/CODE] (stashes foreign maps per-server), [CODE]global[/CODE] (syncs canvas pixel data), or [CODE]untracked[/CODE] (vanilla behavior).
[*][B]sync-blacklist.servers:[/B] List of [I]server-id[/I]s where data should never be loaded or saved.
[*][B]sync-blacklist.worlds:[/B] List of world names where synchronization is temporarily suspended for the player.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]4. Companions / Pets[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]companions.scan-radius:[/B] The maximum distance (in blocks) around a switching player to scan for owned tamed entities to synchronize.
[*][B]companions.mode:[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]follow:[/B] Companions follow the player across servers.
[*][B]return:[/B] Companions stay on the server they were left on, reappearing when the player logs back into that specific server.
[*][B]untracked:[/B] Pets are not synchronized or tracked by the plugin.
[/LIST]
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]5. Prometheus Metrics[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]metrics.enabled:[/B] If true, starts an embedded HTTP server to expose plugin and pool metrics.
[*][B]metrics.port:[/B] Port for Prometheus scraping (default: 8080).
[*][B]metrics.path:[/B] Path for metrics endpoint (default: /metrics).
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5]► Commands & Permissions[/SIZE]

[SIZE=4][B]Administrator Commands[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]/databridge inspect <player> [inventory|enderchest] [--edit][/B]
[LIST]
[*]Opens GUI to view or edit saved player data, inventory, or ender chest.
[*]Left-Click items to view in Safe Read-Only Mode; Right-Click items to open in Interactive Edit Mode.
[*]Works even if the player is offline.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.inspect[/I] / [I]databridge.inspect.edit[/I] (for [I]--edit[/I] or Right-Click)
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge invsee <player> [--edit][/B]
[LIST]
[*]Directly opens saved player inventory view or edit GUI.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.inspect[/I] / [I]databridge.inspect.edit[/I] (for [I]--edit[/I])
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge endersee <player> [--edit][/B]
[LIST]
[*]Directly opens saved player ender chest view or edit GUI.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.inspect[/I] / [I]databridge.inspect.edit[/I] (for [I]--edit[/I])
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge migrate <source> <target>[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Manually move data between two identities (UUID or Name).
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.admin[/I]
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge unlock <player>[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Releases a stuck data lock if a server crashed without releasing it.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.admin[/I]
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge reload[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Reloads the configuration and reconnects to the database pool.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.admin[/I]
[/LIST]
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]Proxy Commands[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]/databridge unlock <player>[/B] (Available on Bungee/Velocity): Releases a data lock across the network.
[*][B]/databridge forceunlock <player>[/B] (Available on Bungee/Velocity): Relays a signal to the backend server to drop the lock immediately.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]Permission Nodes Breakdown[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]databridge.inspect[/B]: Permission to view player data, inventories, and ender chests in safe read-only mode.
[*][B]databridge.inspect.edit[/B]: Elevated permission required to interactively edit inventories and ender chests via [I]--edit[/I] or Right-Click.
[*][B]databridge.admin[/B]: Full administrative access (includes unlock, migrate, reload, forceunlock, inspect, edit).
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5]► Database Schema Information[/SIZE]

For administrators managing the database directly, the plugin maintains the following tables (table prefixes applied if configured):

[SIZE=4][B]1. Lock & Identity Registry Table: [I]player_data[/I][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]uuid[/B] (VARCHAR(36), PK): The unique ID of the player.
[*][B]data[/B] (LONGBLOB): The serialized binary data snapshot (legacy backup).
[*][B]data_checksum[/B] (VARCHAR(64)): SHA-256 integrity hash of the data packet.
[*][B]is_locked[/B] (BOOLEAN): Prevents concurrent writes from multiple servers.
[*][B]locking_server[/B] (VARCHAR(255)): The ID of the server currently holding the lock.
[*][B]lock_timestamp[/B] (BIGINT): Heartbeat timestamp to detect orphaned locks.
[*][B]last_known_name[/B] (VARCHAR(16)): Used for identity tracking and /migrate.
[*][B]identity_hash[/B] (VARCHAR(64)): Salted hash of the Name+UUID+Seed combination for secure identity verification.
[*][B]name_last_updated[/B] (BIGINT): Timestamp of when the player's name was last updated.
[*][B]last_updated[/B] (TIMESTAMP/DATETIME): Auto-updated timestamp of the last lock state change.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]2. Inventories Table: [I]databridge_inventories[/I][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]uuid[/B] (VARCHAR(36), PK): The player's unique ID.
[*][B]inventory_blob[/B] (LONGBLOB/TEXT): Serialized player inventory items.
[*][B]armor_blob[/B] (LONGBLOB/TEXT): Serialized armor items.
[*][B]ender_chest_blob[/B] (LONGBLOB/TEXT): Serialized ender chest items.
[*][B]last_updated[/B] (TIMESTAMP/DATETIME): Auto-updated timestamp.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]3. Statistics Table: [I]databridge_statistics[/I][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]uuid[/B] (VARCHAR(36), PK): The player's unique ID.
[*][B]health[/B] (DOUBLE/REAL): Current health value.
[*][B]food_level[/B] (INT/INTEGER): Current food level.
[*][B]xp_level[/B] (INT/INTEGER): Current experience level.
[*][B]xp_exp[/B] (FLOAT/REAL): Current progress to next level.
[*][B]xp_total[/B] (INT/INTEGER): Total experience points.
[*][B]saturation[/B] (FLOAT/REAL): Food saturation level.
[*][B]exhaustion[/B] (FLOAT/REAL): Food exhaustion level.
[*][B]vanilla_stats_json[/B] (LONGTEXT/TEXT): JSON containing all synchronized vanilla statistics, location, and recipe states.
[*][B]last_updated[/B] (TIMESTAMP/DATETIME): Auto-updated timestamp.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]4. Metadata Table: [I]databridge_metadata[/I][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]uuid[/B] (VARCHAR(36), PK): The player's unique ID.
[*][B]pdc_data[/B] (LONGTEXT/TEXT): Serialized persistent data container (custom NBT tags).
[*][B]advancements[/B] (LONGTEXT/TEXT): Serialized advancements and recipes.
[*][B]last_updated[/B] (TIMESTAMP/DATETIME): Auto-updated timestamp.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]5. Companions Table: [I]databridge_companions[/I][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]uuid[/B] (VARCHAR(36), PK): The player's unique ID.
[*][B]companions_nbt[/B] (LONGTEXT/TEXT): Serialized entity metadata and attributes for player's tamed pets.
[*][B]last_updated[/B] (TIMESTAMP/DATETIME): Auto-updated timestamp.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]6. Maps Table: [I]databridge_maps[/I][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]uuid[/B] (VARCHAR(36), PK): The player's unique ID.
[*][B]maps_nbt[/B] (LONGTEXT/TEXT): Serialized stashed map item snapshots for cross-server return mode.
[*][B]last_updated[/B] (TIMESTAMP/DATETIME): Auto-updated timestamp.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]7. Gamemode Inventories Table: [I]databridge_gamemode_inventories[/I][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]uuid, gamemode[/B] (VARCHAR(36), VARCHAR(16), PK): Composite primary key.
[*][B]inventory_blob[/B] (LONGBLOB/TEXT): Gamemode-specific inventory items.
[*][B]armor_blob[/B] (LONGBLOB/TEXT): Gamemode-specific armor items.
[*][B]ender_chest_blob[/B] (LONGBLOB/TEXT): Gamemode-specific ender chest items.
[*][B]last_updated[/B] (TIMESTAMP/DATETIME): Auto-updated timestamp.
[/LIST]

